<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  HomeKit entitlement (`com.apple.developer.homekit`) is INTENTIONALLY
  omitted. Apple gates HomeKit capability behind the paid Developer
  Program; including it here would break local builds for contributors
  signing with a personal Apple ID team. Without the entitlement,
  `HMHomeManager` simply reports zero homes and `HomeKitSkill` returns
  `noHomeFound` — already handled gracefully (no crash). To enable
  real HomeKit control, add `<key>com.apple.developer.homekit</key>
  <true/>` below in your local fork and ensure your provisioning
  profile includes the HomeKit capability.

  iOS LLM Optimization: Kernel Entitlements
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  The following entitlements significantly improve LLM performance on
  memory-constrained devices and are STRONGLY RECOMMENDED for production builds:
    - com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit
    - com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing

  ⚠️  These require a PAID Apple Developer account.
  Personal/free developer teams cannot use these entitlements.

  See KERNEL_ENTITLEMENTS.md for setup instructions.
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.cz.keksiczek.homehub.shared</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
